.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt ROUTE 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm route
.Nd show and set the default route
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl nqv
.Cm add | Cm change
.Op Fl inet
.Op Fl net
.Cm default
.Ar gateway
.Nm
.Op Fl nqv
.Cm delete
.Op Fl inet
.Op Fl net
.Cm default
.Op Ar gateway
.Nm
.Op Fl nqv
.Cm get
.Op Fl inet
.Cm default | Ar address
.Nm
.Op Fl nqv
.Cm show | Cm flush
.Sh DESCRIPTION
OxideBSD's kernel does not have a routing table yet: an address on one of
an interface's subnets is reached directly, and every other through the
single default route.
.Nm
shows the routes and sets the default one.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm add Cm default Ar gateway
Send everything not on a local subnet to
.Ar gateway ,
an IPv4 address.
It fails if there is a default route already.
.It Cm change Cm default Ar gateway
Replace the default route's gateway.
.It Cm delete Cm default Op Ar gateway
Remove the default route
.Pq only if its gateway is Ar gateway , No when given .
.It Cm get Cm default | Ar address
Show the route to
.Ar address ,
or the default route, in FreeBSD's layout.
.It Cm show
List the routes as
.Ql netstat -rn
does: the default route, each configured interface's subnet, and the host
routes of the interfaces' addresses.
.It Cm flush
Remove the default route.
.El
.Pp
The destination of the default route may be written
.Cm default ,
.Li 0.0.0.0
or
.Li 0.0.0.0/0 ;
.Fl inet ,
.Fl net
and
.Fl netmask Li 0.0.0.0
are accepted and change nothing.
Any other destination is refused with
.Dq only the default route can be set .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Show addresses as numbers.
.Nm
always does; this is accepted for scripts written for the other BSDs.
.It Fl q
Quiet: print nothing on success.
.It Fl v
After a change, show the default route.
.El
.Pp
Only the superuser may change the routes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
The route asked for was not there, or was already.
.It 64
The command line was wrong.
.It 68
The gateway is not an address.
.It 69
The route asked for can't be set: only the default route can.
.It 71
The kernel refused the change.
.It 77
A user other than the superuser asked for a change.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# route add default 10.0.2.2
add net default: gateway 10.0.2.2
$ route -n get default
   route to: default
destination: default
       mask: default
    gateway: 10.0.2.2
        fib: 0
  interface: rl0
      flags: <UP,GATEWAY,DONE,STATIC>
 recvpipe  sendpipe  ssthresh  rtt,msec    mtu        weight    expire
        0         0         0         0      1500         1         0
$ route -n show
Routing tables

Internet:
Destination        Gateway            Flags     Netif
default            10.0.2.2           UGS         rl0
10.0.2.0/24        link#1             U           rl0
10.0.2.15          link#2             UHS         lo0
127.0.0.1          link#2             UH          lo0
# route delete default
delete net default: gateway 10.0.2.2
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr dhclient 8 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
This one is written in Rust for OxideBSD.
.Sh BUGS
Only the default route exists: there is no routing table, no routing socket
and no
.Cm monitor .
The default route is the sysctl
.Va net.inet.ip.default_gateway ,
which
.Nm
reads and sets.
